<item><title>Japan sets January start for new Karuma Bridge</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/ug/japan-sets-january-start-for-new-karuma-bridge-1147f1/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/ug/japan-sets-january-start-for-new-karuma-bridge-1147f1/</guid><category>Uganda</category><description>Ambassador Sasayama said construction is scheduled to begin on January 14, 2027, and Japan is planning a second phase of the Kampala Flyover.</description><pubDate>Thu, 26 Nov 2026 05:00:15 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ug.jpg" length="32020" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ug.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Ugandan MPs demand returns from Malaysia mission&apos;s diplomacy funds</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/ug/ugandan-mps-demand-returns-from-malaysia-mission-s-89998c/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/ug/ugandan-mps-demand-returns-from-malaysia-mission-s-89998c/</guid><category>Uganda</category><description>The eight-member delegation is examining whether taxpayer money sent abroad delivers trade, investment and tourism gains rather than VIP allowances.</description><pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 18:21:29 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ug.jpg" length="32020" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ug.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Kampala traders end closure after Museveni intervenes</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/ug/kampala-traders-end-closure-after-museveni-intervenes-1df4b6/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/ug/kampala-traders-end-closure-after-museveni-intervenes-1df4b6/</guid><category>Uganda</category><description>The shutdown challenged taxes on textiles by weight, customs delays and enforcement by Uganda&apos;s revenue authority.</description><pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 18:01:50 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/ug/kampala-traders-end-closure-after-museveni-intervenes-1df4b6/share.jpg" length="39180" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/ug/kampala-traders-end-closure-after-museveni-intervenes-1df4b6/share.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Uganda launches USh54 billion health project for 550,000 mothers and children</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/ug/uganda-launches-ush54-billion-health-project-for-550-000-1bf6d7/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/ug/uganda-launches-ush54-billion-health-project-for-550-000-1bf6d7/</guid><category>Uganda</category><description>The three-year programme will cover 32 health facilities in 11 areas, with work on maternal care, cancer services and health-worker skills.</description><pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 16:17:32 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ug.jpg" length="32020" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ug.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
